{"abstract":"Our brain is bathed in cerebrospinal fluid (CSF) that is produced by the choroid plexus. CSF serves as a dispersion route for hormones and nutrients, and a conduit for waste clearance. Age-dependent reduction in the CSF secretion rate could influence cerebral waste clearance and thereby promote cognitive deficits in the elderly. Here, we resolve age-dependent modulation of CSF dynamics and choroid plexus function by complementary in vivo determinations of intracranial pressure (ICP) and CSF secretion/absorption rates, combined with transcriptomic, morphological, and metabolic analysis of choroid plexus in aging male rats. ICP and CSF secretion rate and absorption capacity remain stable with age, and the choroid plexus retains its morphology, structural integrity, gene expression, and high metabolic rate across the tested ages. This work supports the significance of choroid plexus function for brain aging and promotes this tissue as a future target for neurodegenerative diseases associated with impaired waste clearance and cognitive decline.","author_count":15,"contributors":["Lolansen, Sara Diana","Révész, Eszter Olga","Andreassen, Søren Norge","Trapp, Marleen","Salio, Chiara","Sassoé-Pognetto, Marco","Andersen, Jens V.","Westi, Emil W.","Toft-Bertelsen, Trine L.","Wardman, Jonathan H.","Lundby, Anne Kristine Meinild","Dela, Flemming","Patrizi, Annarita","Aldana, Blanca I.","MacAulay, Nanna"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-828299"],"filters":{"added":"2025-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Europe, EU","OECD"],"country":["Germany","Italy","Latvia"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","German Cancer Research Center","Heidelberg University ","Riga Stradins University","University of Turin"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CAP"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CAP","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"choroid plexus mediated csf secretion remains stable in aging rats via high and age resistant metabolic activity","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1038/s41467-025-61889-6","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-828299","identifier":[{"id":"001535226600020","type":"wos"},{"id":"105011355025","type":"scopus"},{"id":"40701965","type":"pmid"},{"id":"PMC12287394","type":"pmcid"}],"ids":["ku-09b51431-e36c-4876-b5a1-48f8a99f6dcd"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-3-FBF89E192AFA1BAFE8D3069CBB8985BE"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1038/s41467-025-61889-6","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/458677713/s41467-025-61889-6.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Neuroscience, Molecular Neuroscience"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"capital region of denmark","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-CAP","l3nl":"Capital Region of Denmark","l3nn":"Capital Region of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Capital Region of Denmark","namevar":["Copenhagen University Hospital - Rigshospitalet"],"nora_code":"DI-HO-CAP","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"de","key":"german cancer research center","loc":["Germany","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"German Cancer Research Center","used":1},{"affno":"4","country":"it","key":"uni