{"abstract":"Purpose: Clinical trials have demonstrated efficacy of proprotein convertase subtilisin/kexin type 9 inhibitors (PCSK9i) in reducing risk of cardiovascular disease events, but effectiveness in routine clinical care has not been well-studied. We used negative control outcomes to assess potential confounding in an observational study of PCSK9i versus ezetimibe or high-intensity statin. Methods: Using commercial claims, we identified U.S. adults initiating PCSK9i, ezetimibe, or high-intensity statin in 2015–2018, with other lipid-lowering therapy (LLT) use in the year prior (LLT cohort) or atherosclerotic cardiovascular disease (ASCVD) in the past 90 days (ASCVD cohort). We compared initiators of PCSK9i to ezetimibe and high-intensity statin by estimating one-year risks of negative control outcomes influenced by frailty or health-seeking behaviors. Inverse probability of treatment and censoring weighted estimators of risk differences (RDs) were used to evaluate residual confounding after controlling for covariates. Results: PCSK9i initiators had lower one-year risks of negative control outcomes associated with frailty, such as decubitus ulcer in the ASCVD cohort (PCSK9i vs. high-intensity statin RD = −3.5%, 95% confidence interval (CI): −4.6%, −2.5%; PCSK9i vs. ezetimibe RD = −1.3%, 95% CI: −2.1%, −0.6%), with similar but attenuated associations in the LLT cohort. Lower risks of accidents and fractures were also observed for PCSK9i, varying by cohort. Risks were similar for outcomes associated with health-seeking behaviors, although trended higher for PCSK9i in the ASCVD cohort. Conclusions: Observed associations suggest lower frailty and potentially greater health-seeking behaviors among PCSK9i initiators, particularly those with a recent ASCVD diagnosis, with the potential to bias real-world analyses of treatment effectiveness.","author_count":9,"contributors":["Levintow, Sara N.","Orroth, Kate K.","Breskin, Alexander","Park, Andrew S.","Flores-Arredondo, Jose H.","Dluzniewski, Paul","Navar, Ann Marie","Sørensen, Henrik Toft","Brookhart, M. Alan"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-248135"],"filters":{"added":"2022-04","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["America, North","OECD"],"corresponding_author":["Levintow, Sara N."],"country":["United States"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Amgen Incorporated","Duke University","University of North Carolina","University of Texas at Dallas"],"keyword":["Cardiovascular disease","Cohort study","Comparative analyses","Ezetimibe","Negative control","Residual confounding","Statins"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-OT","DI-U"],"level3":{"OT":["Unspecified organisation"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"use of negative control outcomes to assess the comparability of patients initiating lipid lowering therapies","src":["au"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/85121422563","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-248135","identifier":[{"id":"34894377","type":"pmid"},{"id":"85121422563","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["au-cfe9a6c5-f11d-4cc0-9c39-7a7acc3bb2a4"],"keyword":["cardiovascular disease","cohort study","comparative analyses","ezetimibe","negative control","proprotein convertase subtilisin/kexin type 9 inhibitors","residual confounding","statins"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-1745687B76DBFBD89A3BE597B00A70C5"],"oai":{"class":"Unused","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2022","yearSub":"2022"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"miscellaneous","l2":"DI-OT","l2n":"Miscellaneous","l3":"DI-OT","l3nl":"Other Research","l3nn":"Miscellaneous","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Miscellaneous","namevar":["Unspecified organisation"],"nora_code":"DI-OT","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"us","key":"university of north carolina","loc":["United States","America, North","OECD"],"name":"University of North Carolina","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"us","key":"amgen incorporated","loc":["United States","America, North","OECD"],"name":"Amgen Incorporated","used":1},{"affno":"4","country":"us","key":"university of texas at dallas","loc":["United States","America, North","OECD"],"name":"University of Texas at Dallas","used":1},{"affno":"5","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Health, Department of Clinical Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine - Department of Clinical Epidemiology"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1},{"affno":"6","country":"us","key":"duke university","loc":["United States","America, North","OECD"],"name":"Duke University","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1 2","corresponding":null,"first":"Sara N.","key":"levintowpau","last":"Levintow","name":"Levintow, Sara N.","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"Kate K.","key":"orrothpau","last":"Orroth","name":"Orroth, Kate K.","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 2","corresponding":null,"first":"Alexander","key":"breskinpau","last":"Breskin","name":"Breskin, Alexander","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"Andrew S.","key":"parkpau","last":"Park","name":"Park, Andrew S.","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"Jose H.","key":"floresarredondopau","last":"Flores-Arredondo","name":"Flores-Arredondo, Jose H.","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"Paul","key":"dluzniewskipau","last":"Dluzniewski","name":"Dluzniewski, Paul","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"4","corresponding":null,"first":"Ann Marie","key":"navarpau","last":"Navar","name":"Navar, Ann Marie","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"5","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Henrik T.","key":"sørensenpau","last":"Sørensen","locid":"4d49d93a-4913-4223-ba59-272e717a845d","name":"Sørensen, Henrik Toft","name_org":"Sørensen, Henrik T.","orcid":"0000-0003-4299-7040","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 6","corresponding":null,"first":"M. Alan","key":"brookhartpau","last":"Brookhart","name":"Brookhart, M. Alan","rank":9,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["34894377"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1002/pds.5396","issn":["10538569","10991557"],"issn_org":["10538569"],"issue":"4","journal":"Pharmacoepidemiology and Drug Safety","pages":"383-392","publisher":"John Wiley and Sons Ltd","status":"p","title":"Pharmacoepidemiology and Drug Safety","volume":"31"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85121422563"],"search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Miscellaneous","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-OT","DI-OT-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Miscellaneous","Other Research","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-cfe9a6c5-f11d-4cc0-9c39-7a7acc3bb2a4"],"src":["AU Aarhus University"],"title":"Use of negative control outcomes to assess the comparability of patients initiating lipid-lowering therapies","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-248135","year":"2022","yearsub":"2022"}
{"abstract":"INTRODUCTION: Posthemorrhagic hydrocephalus (PHH) often develops following hemorrhagic events such as intraventricular hemorrhage (IVH) and subarachnoid hemorrhage (SAH). Treatment is limited to surgical diversion of the cerebrospinal fluid (CSF) since no efficient pharmacological therapies are available. This limitation follows from our incomplete knowledge of the molecular mechanisms underlying the ventriculomegaly characteristic of PHH. Here, we aimed to elucidate the molecular coupling between a hemorrhagic event and the subsequent PHH development, and reveal the inflammatory profile of the PHH pathogenesis. METHODS: CSF obtained from patients with SAH was analyzed for inflammatory markers using the proximity extension assay (PEA) technique. We employed an in vivo rat model of IVH to determine ventricular size, brain water content, intracranial pressure, and CSF secretion rate, as well as for transcriptomic analysis. Ex vivo radio-isotope assays of choroid plexus transport were employed to determine the direct effect of choroidal exposure to blood and inflammatory markers, both with acutely isolated choroid plexus and after prolonged exposure obtained with viable choroid plexus kept in tissue culture conditions. RESULTS: The rat model of IVH demonstrated PHH and associated CSF hypersecretion. The Na+/K+-ATPase activity was enhanced in choroid plexus isolated from IVH rats, but not directly stimulated by blood components. Inflammatory markers that were elevated in SAH patient CSF acted on immune receptors upregulated in IVH rat choroid plexus and caused Na+/K+/2Cl- cotransporter 1 (NKCC1) hyperactivity in ex vivo experimental conditions. CONCLUSIONS: CSF hypersecretion may contribute to PHH development, likely due to hyperactivity of choroid plexus transporters. The hemorrhage-induced inflammation detected in CSF and in the choroid plexus tissue may represent the underlying pathology. Therapeutic targeting of such pathways may be employed in future treatment strategies towards PHH patients.","author_count":13,"contributors":["Lolansen, Sara Diana","Rostgaard, Nina","Barbuskaite, Dagne","Capion, Tenna","Olsen, Markus Harboe","Norager, Nicolas H.","Vilhardt, Frederik","Andreassen, Søren Norge","Toft-Bertelsen, Trine L.","Ye, Fenghui","Juhler, Marianne","Keep, Richard F.","MacAulay, Nanna"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-419409"],"filters":{"added":"2022-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["America, North","OECD"],"country":["United States"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","University of Michigan, Ann Arbor"],"keyword":["ADENOSINE TRIPHOSPHATASE","Biomarkers","Cerebrospinal fluid","Choroid plexus","Immune response","Interleukin 6","Intraventricular hemorrhage","Management","Online","Ontology","Posthemorrhagic hydrocephalus","SYSTEM","Secretion","Subarachnoid hemorrhage"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CAP"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CAP","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"posthemorrhagic hydrocephalus associates with elevated inflammation and csf hypersecretion via activation of choroidal transporters","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1186/s12987-022-00360-w","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-419409","identifier":[{"id":"000838667000001","type":"wos"},{"id":"PMC9367104","type":"pmcid"},{"id":"85135811388","type":"scopus"},{"id":"35948938","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["ku-2b985ffb-ac42-49d8-9b93-6bb6a7d53fb2"],"keyword":["ADENOSINE-TRIPHOSPHATASE","Biomarkers","Cerebrospinal fluid","Choroid plexus","INTERLEUKIN-6","Immune response","Intraventricular hemorrhage","MANAGEMENT","ONLINE","ONTOLOGY","PLEXUS","Posthemorrhagic hydrocephalus","SECRETION","SYSTEM","Subarachnoid hemorrhage"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-F2C75986805AA2F9D933677E34F575BB"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1186/s12987-022-00360-w","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/316919362/Posthemorrhagic.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2022","yearSub":"2022"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Neuroscience, Molecular Neuroscience"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"capital region of denmark","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-CAP","l3nl":"Capital Region of Denmark","l3nn":"Capital Region of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Capital Region of Denmark","namevar":["Copenhagen University Hospital - Rigshospitalet"],"nora_code":"DI-HO-CAP","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"us","key":"university of michigan ann arbor","loc":["United States","America, North","OECD"],"name":"University of Michigan, Ann Arbor","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","first":"Sara Diana","key":"lolansenpau","last":"Lolansen","locid":"f255e6e4-bc78-441b-acb8-eddb24c1732d","name":"Lolansen, Sara Diana","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Nina","key":"rostgaardpau","last":"Rostgaard","name":"Rostgaard, Nina","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Dagne","key":"barbuskaitepau","last":"Barbuskaite","locid":"5d7c9154-da5b-4c1d-b7bc-3875a717c1db","name":"Barbuskaite, Dagne","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2 1","first":"Tenna","key":"capionpau","last":"Capion","locid":"