L","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-59d465c4-130f-4dff-9b4c-9e17e92195aa"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"RELICS : Strong Lensing Analysis of the Galaxy Clusters Abell S295, Abell 697, MACS J0025.4-1222, and MACS J0159.8-0849","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-447143","year":"2018","yearsub":"2018"}
{"abstract":"We examined the association between mood disorders and risk of herpes zoster in two case-control studies using data from nationwide Danish registries and practices in the UK Clinical Practice Research Datalink. We included incident zoster cases diagnosed in general practice (using systemic antivirals as a proxy in Denmark) or hospital during 1997-2013 in Denmark (n = 190,671) and during 2000-2013 in the United Kingdom (n = 177,361). We risk-set sampled 4 matched population controls per case. Conditional logistic regression analyses adjusting for zoster risk factors showed that the odds ratios for previous mood disorder among cases versus controls were 1.15 (99% confidence interval (CI): 1.12, 1.19; prevalence 7.1% vs. 6.0%) in Denmark and 1.12 (99% CI: 1.11, 1.14; prevalence 31.6% vs. 29.2%) in the United Kingdom. In Denmark, odds ratios were higher for anxiety (1.23; 99% CI: 1.17, 1.30) and severe stress and adjustment disorder (1.24; 99% CI: 1.18, 1.30) than for depression (1.11; 99% CI: 1.07, 1.14). In the United Kingdom, odds ratios for these conditions were similar: 1.12 (99% CI: 1.10, 1.13), 1.12 (99% CI: 1.10, 1.14), and 1.14 (99% CI: 1.10, 1.19) for depression, anxiety, and severe stress and adjustment disorder, respectively. In conclusion, mood disorders were associated with an increased risk of zoster.","author_count":10,"contributors":["Schmidt, Sigrun A J","Langan, Sinéad M","Pedersen, Henrik S","Schønheyder, Henrik Carl","Thomas, Sara L","Smeeth, Liam","Mansfield, Kathryn E","Sørensen, Henrik T","Forbes, Harriet J","Vestergaard, Mogens"],"cuid":["S02-100.00-007567"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"continent":["Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"country":["United Kingdom"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","London School of Hygiene and Tropical Medicine"],"keyword":["ADULTS","Adjustment disorders","Anxiety","Depression","Diagnoses","Diseases","Epidemiology","Herpes zoster","Journal Article","Psychological stress","Registration","Stress disorders","Vaccine","Virus","simplex"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-AU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"mood disorders and risk of herpes zoster in 000000000002 population based case control studies in denmark and the united kingdom","src":["aau","au"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-AU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/pmc/articles/PMC5968637/pdf/kwx338.pdf","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S02-100.00-007567","identifier":[{"id":"PMC5968637","type":"pmcid"},{"id":"29053820","type":"pmid"},{"id":"85047167773","type":"scopus"},{"id":"000432045400015","type":"wos"}],"ids":["aau-9be62ad8-d2f0-4111-a561-fb667811176a","au-2b9d439d-2806-43c8-863a-e5b27642bc66"],"keyword":["ADULTS","DIAGNOSES","DISEASES","EPIDEMIOLOGY","Journal Article","PSYCHOLOGICAL STRESS","REGISTRATION","SIMPLEX","VACCINE","VIRUS","adjustment disorders","anxiety","depression","herpes zoster","stress disorders"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-5-1C1F09D01F4FE4AADF09EF58151A32FE"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/pmc/articles/PMC5968637/pdf/kwx338.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2018","yearSub":"2018"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Health, Department of Clinical Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine - Department of Clinical Epidemiology"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1},{"affno":"2","count