ll Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["aau-cdbc0d79-74a1-46b4-ad0d-c31162a1b277"],"src":["AAU Aalborg University"],"title":"Partner Bereavement and Risk of Herpes Zoster : Results from Two Population-Based Case-Control Studies in Denmark and United Kingdom","type":"Conference Abstract","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-109767","year":"2016","yearsub":"2016"}
{"abstract":"The essential vitamin biotin is a covalent and tenaciously attached prosthetic group in several carboxylases that play important roles in the regulation of energy metabolism. Here we describe increased acetyl-CoA levels and mitochondrial hyperacetylation as downstream metabolic effects of biotin deficiency. Upregulated mitochondrial acetylation sites correlate with the cellular deficiency of the Hst4p deacetylase, and a biotin-starvation-induced accumulation of Hst4p in mitochondria supports a role for Hst4p in lowering mitochondrial acetylation. We show that biotin starvation and knockout of Hst4p cause alterations in cellular respiration and an increase in reactive oxygen species (ROS). These results suggest that Hst4p plays a pivotal role in biotin metabolism and cellular energy homeostasis, and supports that Hst4p is a functional yeast homologue of the sirtuin deacetylase SIRT3. With biotin deficiency being involved in various metabolic disorders, this study provides valuable insight into the metabolic effects biotin exerts on eukaryotic cells.","author_count":12,"contributors":["Madsen, Christian Toft","Sylvestersen, Kathrine B","Young, Clifford","Buch-Larsen, Sara C.","Poulsen, Jon Wriedt","Andersen, Marianne Agerholm","Palmqvist, Eva A","Hey-Mogensen, Martin","Jensen, Per B.","Treebak, Jonas T.","Lisby, Michael","Nielsen, Michael L."],"cuid":["S01-000.00-543989"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-PR","DI-U"],"level3":{"PR":["DI-PR-ALL","DI-PR-NOVO"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-PR-NOVO","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"biotin starvation causes mitochondrial protein hyperacetylation and partial rescue by the sirt000000000003 like deacetylase hst000000000004p","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1038/ncomms8726","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-543989","identifier":[{"id":"PMC4510963","type":"pmcid"},{"id":"84936992221","type":"scopus"},{"id":"26158509","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["ku-fc335c2d-c319-428d-8e89-1cb0a07f3a3e"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-61DC4873B5290D1126D488A638263212"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1038/ncomms8726","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/155920272/Biotin_starvation_causes_mitochondrial_protein_hyperacetylation_and_partial_rescue_by_the_SIRT3_like_deacetylase_Hst4p.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2015","yearSub":"2015"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Novo Nordisk Foundation Center for Protein Research, Proteomics Program"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"novo nordisk","l2":"DI-PR","l2n":"Private Research","l3":"DI-PR-NOVO","l3nl":"Novo Nordisk","l3nn":"Novo Nordisk","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Novo Nordisk","namevar":["Novo Nordisk"],"nora_code":"DI-PR-NOVO","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","first":"Christian Toft","key":"madsenpau","last":"Madsen","locid":"851c38dd-acbd-4ba1-a44d-c72bd8d0659e","name":"Madsen, Christian Toft","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Kathrine Beck","key":"sylvestersenpau","last":"Sylvestersen","locid":"f01f6dfe-cc78-4707-9b90-b1ac595fcb2e","name":"Sylvestersen, Kathrine B","name_org":"Sylvestersen, Kathrine Beck","orcid":"0000-0002-8201-4769","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Clifford","key":"youngpau","last":"Young","locid":"ebf25d13-dfce-4008-9682-3649c411875b","name":"Young, Clifford","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Sara Charlotte","key":"larsenpau","last":"Larsen","locid":"975fd164-f221-4968-a0d4-1e50e7887842","name":"Buch-Larsen, Sara C.","name_org":"Larsen, Sara Charlotte","orcid":"0000-0001-6250-5467","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Jon Wriedt","key":"poulsenpau","last":"Poulsen","locid":"266bf9ea-8edf-4222-8bc0-17ffbf78ad0b","name":"Poulsen, Jon Wriedt","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","country":"dk","first":"Marianne Agerholm","key":"andersenpau","last":"Andersen","locid":"76ac04eb-ba21-4c19-a12d-bdfc053b558a","name":"Andersen, Marianne Agerholm","orcid":"0000-0001-8687-1031","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Eva A","key":"palmqvistpau","last":"Palmqvist","name":"Palmqvist, Eva A","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Martin","key":"heymogensenpau","last":"Hey-Mogensen","name":"Hey-Mogensen, Martin","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Per B.","key":"jensenpau","last":"Jensen","name":"Jensen, Per B.","rank":9,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Jonas Thue","key":"treebakpau","last":"Treebak","locid":"a648ef82-ccb3-4add-83c1-384e0d90952b","name":"Treebak, Jonas T.","name_org":"Treebak, Jonas Thue","orcid":"0000-0003-1488-7012","rank":10,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Michael","key":"lisbypau","last":"Lisby","locid":"cab97fc6-55a6-4615-af05-d077341b5ae0","name":"Lisby, Michael","orcid":"0000-0002-4830-5247","rank":11,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Michael Lund","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","locid":"b72d98f7-79fa-43a7-8066-783ed8034146","name":"Nielsen, Michael L.","name_org":"Nielsen, Michael Lund","orcid":"0000-0002-0067-9039","rank":12,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["26158509"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1038/ncomms8726","issn":["20411723"],"journal":"Nature Communications","paperid":"7726","status":"p","title":"Nature Communications","volume":"6"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-84936992221"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Private Research","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-PR","DI-PR-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Novo Nordisk","Private Research","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-fc335c2d-c319-428d-8e89-1cb0a07f3a3e"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Biotin starvation causes mitochondrial protein hyperacetylation and partial rescue by the SIRT3-like deacetylase Hst4p","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-543989","year":"2015","yearsub":"2015"}
{"abstract":"Calmodulin (CaM)(1) is the central mediator of intracellular Ca(2+) signalling in cardiomyocytes, where it conveys the intricate Ca(2+) transients to the proteins controlling cardiac contraction. We recently linked two separate mutations in CaM (N53I and N97S) to dominantly inherited catecholaminergic polymorphic ventricular tachycardia (CPVT), an arrhythmic disorder in which exercise or acute emotion can lead to syncope and sudden cardiac death. Given the ubiquitous presence of CaM in all eukaryote cells, it is particular intriguing that carriers of either mutation show no additional symptoms. Here, we investigated the effects of the CaM CPVT mutations in a zebrafish animal model. Three-days old embryos injected with either CaM mRNA showed no detectable pathologies or developmental abnormalities. However, embryos injected with CPVT CaM mRNA displayed increased heart rate compared to WT CaM mRNA under β-adrenergic stimulation, demonstrating a conserved dominant cardiac specific effect between zebrafish and human carriers of these mutations. Motivated by the highly similar physiological phenotypes, we compared the effects of the N53I and N97S mutations on the biophysical and functional properties of CaM. Surprisingly, the mutations have opposing effects on CaM C-lobe Ca(2+) binding affinity and kinetics, and changes to the CaM N-lobe Ca(2+) binding are minor and specific to the N53I mutation. Furthermore, both mutations induce differential perturbations to structure and stability towards unfolding. Our results suggest different molecular disease mechanisms for the CPVT (N53I and N97S mutations), and strongly support that cardiac contraction is the physiological process most sensitive to CaM integrity. This article is protected by copyright. All rights reserved.","author_count":9,"contributors":["Søndergaard, Mads Toft","Sorensen, Anders B","Skov, Louise L","Kjaer-Sorensen, Kasper","Bauer, Mikael C","Nyegaard, Mette","Linse, Sara","Oxvig, Claus","Overgaard, Michael Toft"],"cuid":["S02-100.00-000337"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"continent":["Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"country":["Sweden"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Lund University"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-AU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"calmodulin mutations causing catecholaminergic polymorphic ventricular tachycardia confer opposing functional and biophysical molecular changes","src":["aau","au"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-AU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1111/febs.13184","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S02-100.00-000337","identifier":[{"id":"WOS:000350288300012","type":"wos"},{"id":"84923176771","type":"scopus"},{"id":"25557436","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["aau-06674a8f-9f6e-43b8-a543-923b654539ea","au-9df2db2a-3cec-4fff-824f-6cdadff82d53"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-5-7D54D1C6C5E455BD705B3DAE13B5AABE"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1111/febs.13184","version":"Other Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Unused","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2015","yearSub":"2014"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"aau aalborg university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AAU","l3nl":"Aalborg University","l3nn":"AAU Aalborg University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AAU Aalborg University","namevar":["Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science (ENG)","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science, Department of Chemistry and Bioscience","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science, Department of Chemistry and Bioscience, Section of Biotechnology"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AAU","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Natural Sciences, Department of Molecular Biology and Genetics, Department of Molecular Biology and Genetics - Molecular Intervention"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"se","key":"lund university","loc":["Sweden","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Lund University","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Mads T","key":"søndergaardpau","last":"Søndergaard","locid":"1febcb26-0ee5-44f3-a552-5ec579cc8727","name":"Søndergaard, Mads Toft","name_org":"Søndergaard, Mads T","orcid":"0000-0001-6779-5109","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Anders B","key":"sorensenpau","last":"Sorensen","locid":"af66fd21-fec1-4698-ac1d-0fc6c7dc0d0f","name":"Sorensen, Anders B","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Louise L","key":"skovpau","last":"Skov","locid":"a4c5fa84-eca2-4ccb-8f21-7a30125dce55","name":"Skov, Louise L","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Kasper","key":"kjaersorensenpau","last":"Kjaer-Sorensen","locid":"cedf0a18-d9ff-412a-8631-59cc6e28af15","name":"Kjaer-Sorensen, Kasper","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"Mikael C","key":"bauerpau","last":"Bauer","name":"Bauer, Mikael C","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Mette","key":"nyegaardpau","last":"Nyegaard","locid":"a34df7ff-0fb5-44b0-8255-6dc2c9b962f3","name":"Nyegaard, Mette","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"Sara","key":"linsepau","last":"Linse","name":"Linse, Sara","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Claus","key":"oxvigpau","last":"Oxvig","locid":"ed472b6b-b72e-45f7-9d27-09bc23d0db9d","name":"Oxvig, Claus","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Michael Toft","key":"overgaardpau","last":"Overgaard","locid":"8bd43772-17bb-45d3-9190-b230a7038933","name":"Overgaard, Michael Toft","orcid":"0000-0002-1423-2481","rank":9,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["25557436"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1111/febs.13184","issn":["14321033","1742464X"],"issn_org":["1742464X"],"issue":"4","journal":"FEBS Journal","pages":"803-816","publisher":"Wiley-Blackwell Publishing Ltd","publisher_org":"Wiley-Blackwell Publishing Ltd.","status":"p","title":"FEBS Journal","title_org":"FEBS journal","volume":"282"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-84923176771"],"search":{"DAF":["Aalborg University","Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["aau-06674a8f-9f6e-43b8-a543-923b654539ea","au-9df2db2a-3cec-4fff-824f-6cdadff82d53"],"src":["AAU Aalborg University","AU Aarhus University"],"title":"Calmodulin mutations causing catecholaminergic polymorphic ventricular tachycardia confer opposing functional and biophysical molecular changes","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S02-100.00-000337","year":"2015","yearsub":2015}
{"abstract":"Pregnancy associated plasma protein-A (PAPP-A) functions to increase local insulin-like growth factor (IGF)-I bioactivity. In this study, we used transgenic mice that constitutively express human PAPP-A in arterial smooth muscle to test the hypothesis that overexpression of PAPP-A enhances vascular smooth muscle cell (SMC) response to IGF-I in vivo. PAPP-A transgenic (Tg) and wild-type (WT) mice underwent unilateral carotid ligation, a model of injury-induced SMC hyperplasia and neointimal formation. In both WT and PAPP-A Tg mice, endogenous PAPP-A mRNA expression showed peak elevation five days after carotid ligation. However, PAPP-A Tg mice had 70-75% less neointima than WT at five and ten days post-ligation with a significant reduction in occlusion of the ligated artery. WT and PAPP-A Tg mice had equivalent increases in medial area and vessel remodeling post-ligation. There was little change in medial area and no evidence of neointima in the contralateral carotid of WT or PAPP-A Tg mice. Both WT and PAPP-A Tg carotids exhibited signs of de-differentiation of SMC, which precedes the increase in proliferation and migration that results in neointimal formation. However, the number of proliferating cells in the media and neointima of the ligated PAPP-A Tg artery was reduced by 90% at day 5 post-surgery compared to WT. This decrease was associated with a significant decrease in an in vivo marker of IGF-I bioactivity and reduced IGF-I-stimulated receptor phosphorylation ex vivo. These data suggest differential effects of chronic (transgenic) and transient (endogenous) PAPP-A expression on neointimal formation following vascular injury that may be due, in part, to differential impact on IGF-I signaling.","author_count":5,"contributors":["Bale, Laurie K","Resch, Zachary T","Harstad, Sara L","Overgaard, Michael Toft","Conover, Cheryl A."],"cuid":["S01-000.00-111592"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["America, North","OECD"],"country":["United States"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Mayo Clinic Rochester, MN"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AAU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"constitutive expression of pregnancy associated plasma protein a in arterial smooth muscle reduces the vascular response to injury in vivo","src":["aau"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1152/ajpendo.00376.2012","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-111592","identifier":[{"id":"WOS:000313614700003","type":"wos"},{"id":"84872386376","type":"scopus"},{"id":"23169786","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["aau-d3edb049-375a-477e-b901-6f837e28ba3a"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-4BE58A60920B6057B278745501E391EF"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1152/ajpendo.00376.2012","version":"Other Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Unused","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2013","yearSub":"2013"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"aau aalborg university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AAU","l3nl":"Aalborg University","l3nn":"AAU Aalborg University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AAU Aalborg University","namevar":["Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science (ENG)","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science, Department of Chemistry and Bioscience","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science, Department of Chemistry and Bioscience, Section of Biotechnology"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AAU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"us","key":"mayo clinic rochester mn","loc":["United States","America, North","OECD"],"name":"Mayo Clinic Rochester, MN","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first"